eption_prompting. Generative Agents (p.47): 'Whether the Generative Agents system generates believable behavior is evaluated with the help of 100 human evaluators.' They ranked believability of communication patterns in four categories (remember, plan, react, reflect) across four architectures; the full architecture performed best, though erratic behavior and hallucination appeared. Also covered: creator-critic pairs, Constitutional AI, multi-agent debate, MAD with a judge, round-table confidence-weighted voting, AutoGen, ChatEval, Sotopia, GovSim. Related 'Simulating 1000 People' recruited 1052 humans for interview-based agent profiles.\", evidence_ids=[\"ev-f03e4b7f1b7fc6e66886\"], section=\"multi_agent\")", "observations": "Execution logs:\nLast output from code snippet:\n{'note_id': 'multi_agent', 'sources': ['paper.pdf'], 'chars': 1027}", "observations_images": null, "action_output": {"note_id": "multi_agent", "sources": ["paper.pdf"], "chars": 1027}, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 8988, "output_tokens": 363, "total_tokens": 9351}, "is_final_answer": false}}
