{"event": "tool_call", "time": 1793333839.61363, "run_id": "6b1ee4ab9a424b1c9a5b89e5f5a5b4f8", "seq": 329, "tool": "write_note", "arguments": {"title": "outlook", "content": "Outlook notes (pp.51-52). Table 4 (p.51) lists five research agenda topics with challenges: 'Training Data' (finetune with inference-time reasoning data, convergent/stable RL, VLA/multimodal speech), 'Hallucination' (self verification, mechanistic interpretability, open-ended/open-world models), 'Agent Behavior' (scalable simulation infrastructure and role playing, distill reasoning to small models, models of agent/human behavior and emergent behavior), 'Self reflection' (in-model self reflection and metareasoning, metacognition/personality, automated scientific discovery) and 'Safety' (responsibility/liability, privacy/fairness, wider application areas). So agenda_topics = training_data, hallucination, agent_behavior, self_reflection, safety. Conclusion (Sec.5.2, p.52): 'Robotic interaction and tool-use build on grounded retrieval augmentation, social interaction (such as theory of mind) builds on self reflection, and all categories benefit from reasoning and self-verification.' So shared_foundations = reasoning, self_verification. Safety (p.51) calls for multi-layer safeguards, continual adversarial training and red-teaming, self-regulation, and benchmarks such as AgentHarm.", "evidence_ids": ["ev-99f0f0a37d328bfed1a9", "ev-01ce8948bcc88d235ea3"], "section": "outlook"}}
{"event": "section_note", "time": 1793333839.613716, "run_id": "6b1ee4ab9a424b1c9a5b89e5f5a5b4f8", "seq": 330, "section": "outlook", "pages": [51, 52], "content": "Outlook notes (pp.51-52). Table 4 (p.51) lists five research agenda topics with challenges: 'Training Data' (finetune with inference-time reasoning data, convergent/stable RL, VLA/multimodal speech), 'Hallucination' (self verification, mechanistic interpretability, open-ended/open-world models), 'Agent Behavior' (scalable simulation infrastructure and role playing, distill reasoning to small models, models of agent/human behavior and emergent behavior), 'Self reflection' (in-model self reflection and metareasoning, metacognition/personality, automated scientific discovery) and 'Safety' (responsibility/liability, privacy/fairness, wider application areas). So agenda_topics = training_data, hallucination, agent_behavior, self_reflection, safety. Conclusion (Sec.5.2, p.52): 'Robotic interaction and tool-use build on grounded retrieval augmentation, social interaction (such as theory of mind) builds on self reflection, and all categories benefit from reasoning and self-verification.' So shared_foundations = reasoning, self_verification. Safety (p.51) calls for multi-layer safeguards, continual adversarial training and red-teaming, self-regulation, and benchmarks such as AgentHarm."}
{"event": "tool_result", "time": 1793333839.6137671, "run_id": "6b1ee4ab9a424b1c9a5b89e5f5a5b4f8", "seq": 331, "action": {"tool": "write_note", "title": "outlook", "content": "Outlook notes (pp.51-52). Table 4 (p.51) lists five research agenda topics with challenges: 'Training Data' (finetune with inference-time reasoning data, convergent/stable RL, VLA/multimodal speech), 'Hallucination' (self verification, mechanistic interpretability, open-ended/open-world models), 'Agent Behavior' (scalable simulation infrastructure and role playing, distill reasoning to small models, models of agent/human behavior and emergent behavior), 'Self reflection' (in-model self reflection and metareasoning, metacognition/personality, automated scientific discovery) and 'Safety' (responsibility/liability, privacy/fairness, wider application areas). So agenda_topics = training_data, hallucination, agent_behavior, self_reflection, safety. Conclusion (Sec.5.2, p.52): 'Robotic interaction and tool-use build on grounded retrieval augmentation, social interaction (such as theory of mind) builds on self reflection, and all categories benefit from reasoning and self-verification.' So shared_foundations = reasoning, self_verification. Safety (p.51) calls for multi-layer safeguards, continual adversarial training and red-teaming, self-regulation, and benchmarks such as AgentHarm.", "evidence_ids": ["ev-99f0f0a37d328bfed1a9", "ev-01ce8948bcc88d235ea3"], "section": "outlook"}, "result": {"note_id": "outlook", "sources": ["paper.pdf"], "chars": 1195}}
