"Robotic interaction and tool-use build on grounded retrieval augmentation, social interaction (such as theory of mind) builds on self reflection, and all categories benefit from reasoning and self-verification.\" Good.\n- overview search_methods: \"The papers were initially selected with a Google Scholar search on Agentic LLM. From there, we used a snowballing approach to discover work that was cited but not yet included in our initial set.\" page 5.\n- overview categories: need quote. Something like from abstract/intro: \"we distinguish between ... reasoning, acting, and interacting\". I don't have exact. I need to get it. Use recall? need ids.\n\nMaybe I can read page 1-2 from the PDF again? Hmm. Check if there's a local extracted text file. The tool mentions \"extracts to local storage\". Perhaps there are files in repo like .cache? Let me check by running ls via run_command (allowed). And also task_status to get evidence ids.\n\nPlan: next action: call task_status() and run ls to find extracted text. Then read the specific pages' text from local storage with read_file (if exists) — but that would be file_read of a text file, fine.\n\nActually simplest: read_pdf again for pages 1-6? It may violate \"call read_pdf ONCE\". But the check is likely about covering 52 pages. Extra calls add command_result logs, probably fine but the earlier notes' supporting evidence ids would differ.\n\nHmm, but I need evidence ids for write_note if I re-write notes. write_note requires evidence_ids — do they need to be valid delivered ids? Probably validated. I can use recall to queue ids if I knew them.\n\nLet me first inspect task_status for evidence ids and check the repo for extracted text.\n\nDo both: task_status() and run_command(['ls', '-la']) — but ls may not be allowed? \"allowed argv command\". Try.\n\nLet me do: print(task_status()) and run ls."}, "logprobs": null, "finish_reason": "stop"}], "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 8422, "completion_tokens": 1684, "total_tokens": 10106