f6385e0a370da21ad7d6fe029d7fb8c", "locator": "page:50", "required": true, "page": 50, "valid": true, "atomic": true, "chars": 4663, "exposed": true}, {"id": "ev-99f0f0a37d328bfed1a9", "source": "paper.pdf", "version": "b4767423c79db69ae7138f4c0aed7733af6385e0a370da21ad7d6fe029d7fb8c", "locator": "page:51", "required": true, "page": 51, "valid": true, "atomic": true, "chars": 3844, "exposed": true}, {"id": "ev-01ce8948bcc88d235ea3", "source": "paper.pdf", "version": "b4767423c79db69ae7138f4c0aed7733af6385e0a370da21ad7d6fe029d7fb8c", "locator": "page:52", "required": true, "page": 52, "valid": true, "atomic": true, "chars": 4072, "exposed": true}], "notes": {"overview": {"id": "overview", "content": "Overview notes (pp.1-6). Agentic LLMs are defined as agents that receive natural-language input, reason, act and interact; the survey is organized by the three categories reason / act / interact (categories answer). The three build on each other: reasoning technology enables acting by assistants, acting/interaction enables social simulation, and outcomes feed data augmentation to finetune LLMs (virtuous circle, Fig.1, p.4). Literature selection (Sec.1.2, p.5): 'The papers were initially selected with a Google Scholar search on Agentic LLM. From there, we used a snowballing approach to discover work that was cited but not yet included in our initial set.' So search_methods = google_scholar, snowballing. Only LLM-based approaches kept; most works 2024, some 2023/2025. Sec.1.3 training pipeline (pretrain, SFT, instruction tuning, alignment RLHF/DPO/RLVR, in-context learning); Sec.1.4 motivates agentic LLMs with four challenges: prompt engineering, hallucination, ...", "sources": ["paper.pdf"], "evidence_ids": ["ev-26c94297c50e4ef408a2", "ev-dbca06e364385e22f3c5", "ev-89534f70bedf0ab45dc5"], "valid": true, "request": 5}, "reasoning": {"id": "reasoning", "content": "Reasoning notes (final). Self-Consistency (Sec.2.1.1, p.10): 'Self Consistency is an ensemble approach that samples diverse reasoning paths, evaluates them, and selects the most consistent answer using majority voting.' So self_consistency_selection = majority voting over sampled reasoning paths' answers; it lifts CoT by 10-20 points and underpins o1/o3/DeepSeek/Qwen. Tree of Thoughts (Sec.2.1.3, p.13): 'The paper describes both a breadth-first and a depth-first controller.' So tot_search = breadth_first, depth_first; ToT adds an external search controller with generation + evaluation prompts and backtracking. Graph of Thoughts generalizes to graph-structured thoughts. CoT alone is greedy single-path; Self-Consistency/ToT build on CoT.", "sources": ["paper.pdf"], "evidence_ids": ["ev-d2b420a2b23cdc8166d3", "ev-4049593a30e2846f8394"], "valid": true, "request": 10}, "tool_use": {"id": "tool_use", "content": "Tool-use notes (p.21-23). Acting via tools: Toolformer (Schick et al.) is trained to decide which APIs to call, when, with what arguments, and how to use the results (p.23). Tested tools: 'A range of tools is tested: a calculator, a question-answering system, a search engine, a translation system, and a calendar.' so toolformer_tools = calculator, question_answering, search_engine, translation, calendar. ToolBench: 'ToolBench [Qin et al., 2023] contains 16,464 APIs from RapidAPI' -> toolbench_api_count = 16464. Related: EasyTool builds structured tool instructions on ToolBench; ToolAlpaca (3938 instances, 400 APIs); Gorilla/APIBench; planner-caller-summarizer framework with three LLMs (Fig.13). Pages 21-22 cover embodied/VLA robots, SayCan, Inner Monologue, zero-shot object navigation.", "sources": ["paper.pdf"], "evidence_ids": ["ev-731fa63b8d34dde45e62"], "valid": true, "request": 13}, "multi_agent": {"id": "multi_agent", "content": "Multi-agent notes (final, pp.36-37,47). CAMEL (Sec.4.2.2, p.37): two LLMs take predefined roles and 'cooperatively drive a conversation without continuous human prompting. By using inception prompting and role descriptions, the agents stay in character and collaborate toward the goal by breaking down complex problems in manageable steps through dialogue.' So camel_prompting = inception_prompting. Generative Agents (p.47): 'Whether the Generative Agents system generates believable behavior is evaluated with the help of 100 human evaluators.' They ranked believability of communication patterns in four categories (remember, plan, react, reflect) across four architectures; the full architecture performed best, though erratic behavior and hallucination appeared. Also covered: creator-critic pairs, Constitutional AI, multi-agent debate, MAD with a judge, round-table confidence-weighted voting, AutoGen, ChatEval, Sotopia, GovSim. Related 'Simulating 1000 People' recruited 1052 humans for interview-based agent profiles.", "sources": ["paper.pdf"], "evidence_ids": ["ev-f03e4b7f1b7fc6e66886"], "valid": true, "request": 23}, "outlook": {"id": "outlook", "content": "Outlook notes (pp.51-52). Table 4 (p.51) lists five research agenda topics with challenges: 'Training Data' (finetune with inference-time reasoning data, convergent/stable RL, VLA/multimodal speech), 'Hallucination' (self verification, mechanistic interpretability, open-ended/open-world models), 'Agent Behavior' (scalable simulation infrastructure and role playing, distill reasoning to small models, models of agent/human behavior and emergent behavior), 'Self reflection' (in-model self reflection and metareasoning, metacognition/personality, automated scientific discovery) and 'Safety' (responsibility/liability, privacy/fairness, wider application areas). So agenda_topics = training_data, hallucination, agent_behavior, self_reflection, safety. Conclusion (Sec.5.2, p.52): 'Robotic interaction and tool-use build on grounded retrieval augmentation, social interaction (such as theory of mind) builds on self reflection, and all categories benefit from reasoning and self-verification.' So shared_foundations = reasoning, self_verification. Safety (p.51) calls for multi-layer safeguards, continual adversarial training and red-teaming, self-regulation, and benchmarks such as AgentHarm.", "sources": ["paper.pdf"], "evidence_ids": ["ev-99f0f0a37d328bfed1a9", "ev-01ce8948bcc88d235ea3"], "valid": true, "request": 25}}}}
